gearbench (1.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The first public release.
  * A first install starts the service in each desktop session already
    open, so the devices work without logging out, and a removal stops it
    first, which hands the keyboard back.
  * The window has a banner while Gearbench's GNOME Shell extension is not
    running, with Turn on while it is off.
  * About 530 fixes from a review of every line of the program, 36 of them
    for security: devices posing as supported ones are refused, files from
    G HUB and profile packs are read within tighter limits, and messages
    name the device, the cause and what to do.

 -- wmuschetto <113629853+wmuschetto@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:38:10 +0000

